listitem.para:

                  ParameterValue
                - 
Maps to the TR-069 {@code ParameterValueStruct}

section.para:
Any {@code MAP} and {@code LIST} node must include a
{@link ParameterInfo} for the corresponding {@code NumberOfEntries}
parameter.

formalpara.para:
TR069Exception– If the fault is caused by an invalid ParameterPath value, the Invalid Parameter Name fault code (9005) MUST be used instead of the more general Invalid Arguments fault code (9003). A ParameterPath value must be considered invalid if it is not an empty string and does not exactly match a parameter or object name currently present in the data model. If {@code nextLevel} is {@code true} and {@code objectOrTablePath} is a parameter path rather than an object/table path, the method must return a fault response with the Invalid Arguments fault code (9003). If the value cannot be gotten for some reason, this method can generate the following fault codes::
9001 {@link TR069Exception#REQUEST_DENIED}
9002 {@link TR069Exception#INTERNAL_ERROR}
9003 {@link TR069Exception#INVALID_ARGUMENTS}
9005 {@link TR069Exception#INVALID_PARAMETER_NAME}

              TR069Exception– The following fault codes are defined for this
        method: 9001, 9002, 9003, 9004, 9005.



9001 {@link TR069Exception#REQUEST_DENIED}



